From a4c9e11c2061bc46c614ba1690235a1fe81103ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:12:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/57] hw/mchp, hw/avr: generated AVR64EA48 register tables
 and descriptor

generator/atdf2qemu.py now reads 8-bit AVR ATDFs (architecture AVR8X):
per-IP constants and register tables as for Arm parts, plus
include/hw/avr/avr64ea48_gen.h (data and program memory segments,
instances, interrupt vectors by instance) and hw/avr/avr64ea48_device.h
(MchpAvrDeviceInfo: signature, memory sizes, SYSCFG.REVID per silicon
revision, data rows from the profile). mchp_device.h gains the AVR types
(MchpAvrVector, MchpAvrDataRow, MchpAvrDeviceInfo).

Sources: AVR64EA48.atdf (AVR-Ex_DFP 2.8.189), overlays for USART,
CPUINT, CLKCTRL and NVMCTRL, profiles/avr64ea48.yaml. Generated; do not
edit.

Peripheral Pretender: AI-assisted, not for upstream QEMU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
